# Devin ACU Hardening — Reference Playbook
**Production standard, v1.0 — repo-agnostic**

Applies to any repository onboarded to Devin, with or without a graph-based retrieval CLI. Placeholders are written as `<ANGLE_BRACKETS>`; everything else is drop-in.

---

## Part 0 — The cost model (why any of this works)

ACUs accrue on work Devin performs: planning, **context gathering**, execution, browser actions, code execution — plus a small VM/bandwidth component. Cloning repos, waiting for your reply, and waiting for test suites are **not** billed. Sessions auto-sleep after roughly 0.1 ACU of inactivity and cost nothing while asleep.

Three exploitable properties follow:

1. **Retrieval is billed; retrieval you pre-compute is not.** A structured query that returns a call chain replaces a multi-file read plus the planning turns needed to reconcile them.
2. **Snapshot work is free; in-session discovery is billed.** Toolchain installs, warm dependency caches, and index builds cost zero ACUs in the blueprint. The same work discovered mid-session is billed *and* triggers re-planning.
3. **Context size compounds.** Tokens gathered early ride along in every subsequent planning step. Bloat is a per-turn tax, not a one-time charge.

Session-size thresholds (from Session Insights) — size is `max(ACU-derived, message-derived)`:

| Size | ACU (standard) | ACU (enterprise) | User messages |
|---|---|---|---|
| XS | ≤ 2 | ≤ 20 | ≤ 2 |
| S | ≤ 5 | ≤ 50 | ≤ 5 |
| M | ≤ 10 | ≤ 100 | ≤ 10 |
| L | ≤ 20 | ≤ 200 | ≤ 20 |
| XL | > 20 | > 200 | > 20 |

L and XL are flagged unhealthy by Cognition's own tooling. **Target: XS/S/M ≥ 85% of sessions.**

