## Part 5 — Prompt contract

Front-load everything. Facts you supply are free; facts the agent discovers are billed.

```
REPO: <org/repo>   BRANCH: <base-branch>
SCOPE: only these paths — <path/a>, <path/b>. Do not modify anything else.

TASK
<one sentence, imperative>

CONTEXT (given — do not go looking for this)
- Current state: <exact versions / code / error output>
- Target state: <exact target>
- Reference implementation: <file already doing this correctly>
- Known gotcha: <the thing that otherwise costs 4 ACUs>

DECISIONS ALREADY MADE (do not re-evaluate)
- <decision 1>
- <decision 2>

VERIFY
1. `<exact build command>`
2. `<exact test command>`
3. `<exact lint command>`

DONE WHEN
- All three pass
- Diff touches only the scoped paths
- PR opened against <branch>

BUDGET
Target ≤ <N> ACUs. If not converging after two failed attempts at the same step,
STOP, do not try a third approach, and report: what you tried, the exact error,
and what you need from me.

FORBIDDEN
- Do not refactor unrelated code
- Do not upgrade dependencies not named above
- Do not use the browser unless <condition>
- Do not disable, skip, or weaken tests
```

The last forbidden line matters more than it looks. Without it, "make the tests pass" invites the cheapest-path failure — you pay ACUs for a PR you then reject.

