## Part 6 — Playbook template

Register with a macro (`!<name>`) so anyone attaches it with one token. Playbooks are versioned and revertible — treat them as code.

```
Playbook: <NAME>

## Overview
<One paragraph: outcome, and that this is mechanical not design work.>
Target: XS/S session.

## Required From User
- <input 1>
- <input 2>

## Procedure
1. <Refresh index.>
2. <Query by identifier to scope. Do not grep.>
3. <Make the change, single module.>
4. <Build the named module only.>
5. <On failure: refresh index, query the break, fix only what the change caused.>
6. <Run the module test suite.>
7. <If an unrelated test fails, stop and report.>
8. <Open PR with verification evidence and tracker key.>

## Specifications
- Diff confined to the named module
- <postcondition 2>
- Build and tests pass
- PR body contains verification evidence

## Advice and Pointers
- The snapshot has the toolchain installed and caches warm. Do not reinstall or
  reconfigure anything.
- Query by identifier. Prose queries are low-yield on this repo.
- <repo-specific prior correction>

## Forbidden Actions
- Do not modify the root build file or sibling modules
- Do not disable, skip, or weaken any test
- Do not run a full workspace build
- Do not use the browser
- Do not open or parse the index artifact
- Do not attempt a third approach after two failures — stop and report
```

One step per line, imperative, mutually exclusive and collectively exhaustive. Cover setup, task, and delivery.

