## Part 7 — Measurement harness

Do not roll everything at once. You will not be able to attribute the delta, and you will be asked to.

**Control design.** Take 20 comparable work items. Randomize into two arms of 10. Arm A: current configuration. Arm B: hardened AGENTS.md + blueprint + auto-approve + playbook. Same reviewers, same week, same repo.

**Instrumentation** (v3 API):

| Endpoint | Metric |
|---|---|
| `GET /consumption/daily/sessions` | ACU per session |
| `GET /sessions/insights` | Size distribution, issue labels, message counts |
| `GET /metrics/sessions-by-category` | ACU by task category |
| `GET /metrics/prs` | Merged PRs — the denominator |

Tag every session (`<initiative>`, `arm-a` / `arm-b`) so attribution is automatic.

**Primary metric: ACU per *merged* PR.** Not per session — a change that halves session cost while doubling rejections is a regression, and only the merged denominator catches it.

**Quality guardrails — the run fails if any move the wrong way:**

| Guard | Threshold |
|---|---|
| PR rejection rate | No increase vs Arm A |
| Review comments per PR | No increase |
| Post-merge defect rate (30d) | No increase |
| Sessions ending in stop-and-report | ≤ 15% |

That last one is the tuning dial. The bounded fallback is deliberately aggressive; if the agent stops too often, loosen the file cap in Rule 8b from 3 to 5 before touching anything else.

