## Part 8 — Task selection (applies before any of the above)

No amount of instruction tuning rescues a badly chosen task.

Slice criteria:
- Under **90 minutes** of equivalent manual engineering work
- **Atomic**: one file, one module, one CVE, one endpoint
- **Independently verifiable**: tests, build, CI, or a verification script
- **Backwards compatible**: mergeable alone, no coordination with sibling slices
- **Minimal external dependencies**

Wide-and-shallow beats tall-and-deep. Ten XS sessions at 2 ACUs each is cheaper *and* more reliable than one XL session at 35. There are no concurrency limits on Team/Enterprise — run them in parallel.

| Bad slice | Good slice |
|---|---|
| "Remediate all CVEs in this repo" | "Bump `<artifact>` to `<version>` in `<module>`, resolve compile breaks, CI green" |
| "Migrate the service to `<framework vN>`" | "Migrate `<old>` → `<new>` imports in `<module>` only; no behavior change; tests pass" |
| "Fix the flaky tests" | "`<TestClass>.<testMethod>` is flaky. Reproduce with 20 runs, fix the race, keep all other tests green" |

